utral imbalance with an ultra-tight 0.28 bps spread, and 7-day average volume is running 26% above the 30-day average, indicating rising interest. This profile suggests a mix of institutional and sophisticated retail flow, with ample liquidity for large blocks.\n\n**LEVERS:** Funding rates are negligible at 1.37% annualized, and OI/Mcap stands at a moderate 9.9%. Longs are not crowded, leaving ample room for fresh leverage to enter without immediate squeeze risk, though a breakout could trigger a short squeeze given the negative funding baseline.\n\n**RISK:** The #1 risk is a sharp mean-reversion correction from overbought technicals\u2014price is 52% above the 50-day SMA and RSI is deep in overbought territory. A swift 15\u201320% pullback to the $60\u2013$65 zone would be historically normal and would not break the uptrend.\n\n**Accumulate HYPE on a pullback to the $60\u2013$65 support band, where structural buybacks and institutional narrative provide a floor; wait for RSI to cool below 70 before adding size to avoid chasing overextended momentum.**"
